# Handout 3: Presenting and Analyzing Your Data

You collected one week of **baseline** data and three weeks of **intervention**
data. Enter each week below as **seven numbers, Sunday through Saturday**, in
whatever units you tracked — separated by commas.

Enter the number only, not the unit: `6.5, 5, 7, 6, 8, 7.5, 9`, not
`6.5 hours, 5 hours`. If you missed a day, enter `0`. Your graph in 1c is
built from exactly these numbers, so they are worth getting right.
    </Markdown>

    <Markdown id="bmod_h3_recall">
**Your goal behavior:** {{@bmod_h1_q2_response.value}}

**How you said you would measure it:** {{@bmod_h1_q3_measurable.value}}
    </Markdown>

    <DerivedChecks id="bmod_h3_data_checks"
                   slots="baseline_data:Baseline week's data present@1|week_1_data:Week 1 data present@1|week_2_data:Week 2 data present@1|week_3_data:Week 3 data present@1"
